# nw_ses_send_fd() does not zero its control buffer, so the cmsg padding
# bytes handed to sendmsg() are uninitialised. Harmless on Linux, listed in
# docs/REVIEW.md (L3). Remove this once the buffer is memset.
{
   nw_ses_send_fd_cmsg_padding
   Memcheck:Param
   sendmsg(msg.msg_control)
   ...
   fun:nw_ses_send_fd
}
